description:
Warnings when description and code disagree (codes picked after docair-4wk.6):

- an operation that no code in its service serves, when the service has code (never for external parts);
- a route served in a described service that its description lacks; [[import.api]] ignore silences single routes;
- an operationId that names a function in the service whose route differs: W103 stale (ADAPTERS.md §6: the code wins);
- a hint when the operations are served in another service: "set part_of".

API descriptions (OpenAPI, AsyncAPI) declare rendezvous points with their types: the HTTP routes a service offers, the topics it sends and receives. docair reads them as one more adapter that produces facts (ADAPTERS.md §4); the core matches them with what the code serves and requests (§7). Then:

- a handler gets its operation's text and types;
- a caller's line gets what it sends and gets back, with the description as evidence;
- an operation nobody implements shows as an endpoint;
- description and code that disagree warn.

Builds on the adapters epic docair-4wk: the facts model (docair-4wk.2) and cross-language HTTP matching (docair-4wk.6). Exports (Mermaid, LikeC4, Backstage, Structurizr) are left out for now.

design:
Fixture e2e/fixtures/apis:
- api/Cargo.toml declares orders-api (placement by directory);
- api/src/lib.rs: create_order POST /api/orders; get_order GET /api/orders/{orderId} (the description says {id}); update_order PUT /api/order/{id} (stale route, Import 3); list_orders GET /api/orders (undescribed, Import 3);
- api/openapi.yaml: 3.1, servers [{url: /api}], createOrder, getOrder, update_order, cancelOrder (no handler);
- ui/src/cart.ts: a request for POST /api/orders without payload words, and one for POST /v1/charges;
- vendor/payments-openapi.json: title Payments, several operations, one called; docs/payments.md declares payments as external.
